\pard\b The Transformer Architecture\b0\par
\par
This paper introduces a novel neural network architecture called the Transformer. Unlike previous approaches that relied on \i recurrent neural networks\i0  (RNNs), the Transformer uses a mechanism called \b self-attention\b0  to process all words in a sequence simultaneously.\par
\par
\b Key Contributions:\b0\par
1. Scaled Dot-Product Attention\par
2. Multi-Head Attention with 8 parallel heads\par
3. Positional Encoding using sinusoidal functions\par
\par
The model achieves \b 28.4 BLEU\b0  on English-to-German translation, surpassing all previous results. Training took only \i 12 hours\i0  on 8 GPUs, compared to weeks for competing models.\par
\par
This architecture became the foundation for modern large language models including GPT and BERT.\par
